    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0457" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/402: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-08T18:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1930—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>136. Your 167, December 6, 3 p.m. Please orally inform President Moncada that the
                    Department is gratified with his decision to have the boundary protocol signed
                    without further negotiations the end of this month,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d357-f1"/> and that in accordance with his suggestion the Legation
                    at Tegucigalpa is being instructed by cable to inform the Government of Honduras
                    and to suggest that the Honduran representative be appointed in order that he
                    may proceed to Managua with full powers to sign the protocol as has now been
                    fully agreed upon between the two Governments.</p>
                <p>The desire of the Government of Nicaragua to avoid publicity is being brought to
                    the attention of the Honduran Government.</p>
                <p>Please modify appropriately such action as you take under the Department’s
                    telegram 135, December 5, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>The Department believes it now will be unnecessary for Major Geyer to go to
                    Managua on this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="2" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>The protocol was signed at Managua January 21, 1931.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
